---
description: Issue processing rules for fix-issue command
---
# Issue Processing Rules

## Input Parsing Rules
Parse $ARGUMENTS for issue specification:
- Single issue: "123" -> ["123"]
- Range syntax: "105-110" -> ["105", "106", "107", "108", "109", "110"] (format: START-END)
- Space-separated: "105 106 107" -> ["105", "106", "107"]
- Comma-separated: "123,124,125" -> ["123", "124", "125"]
- Single issue: Single number -> ["$ARGUMENTS"]

## Validation Rules
1. Each number must be positive integer > 0
2. Filter out: 0, negative numbers, non-numeric strings
3. Deduplicate issues: Convert to Set, back to sorted Vec
4. Pre-flight check: gh api "repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{num}" for each issue
5. Skip issues that don't exist or are closed
6. Log skipped issues to output/issue-fix-artifacts/skipped_issues.json

## Output Format Rules
Each finding outputs to `docs/outputs/issues/{category}/{filename}.md`:
```yaml
---
title: [P1] Clear title under 70 characters
problem: One sentence describing the issue
impact: One sentence on user/system impact
reproduction: Steps to reproduce or observe
acceptance_criteria:
- Criterion 1
- Criterion 2
effort: 1-5 scale
risk: High|Medium|Low
category: security|critical|performance|reliability|testing|tech-debt
files:
- src/file.rs
labels: security|crash|performance|error-handling|testing|debt
---
```

## Merged Issue Template
When findings > $ARGUMENTS, merge by same file → same category → same risk → related functionality:
```yaml
---
title: [P1] Consolidated: {primary_title}
merged_from: "{count} findings merged"
problems:
- {problem 1}
- {problem 2}
impact: Combined impact
reproduction: |
  Finding 1: {reproduction 1}
  Finding 2: {reproduction 2}
acceptance_criteria:
- Combined criterion
effort: {highest effort}
risk: {highest risk}
category: {primary category}
files:
- {all unique files}
labels: {all unique labels}
source_files:
- docs/outputs/issues/{category}/{file1}.md
- docs/outputs/issues/{category}/{file2}.md
---
```

## Batch Processing Rules
1. ONE PR only when ALL issues are 100% complete and validated
2. NO partial PRs
3. Sequential issue processing, parallel cluster processing
4. If ANY issue fails, batch FAILS - no partial PRs
5. If ANY issue fails after all reconciliations: BATCH FAILS, NO PR created

## Transient Failure Handling
Retry up to 3 times with 5s backoff for:
- gh api network errors
- cargo lock contention ("Blocking waiting for file lock")
- Subagent timeouts (>5min)
